course: dictionary
lesson: 4923
title: Impact: a hit or an effect
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Impact is a noun with two main meanings. It can be a strong hit of one thing against another, as in «the impact of the crash». It can also be a strong effect or influence, as in «Exercise has a good impact on health».
explain: Use the words around it to choose the meaning. Ask: is something crashing or hitting? Then it means a hit. Ask: is something changing or affecting something else? Then it means an effect. Put your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: As a verb, to impact means to have an effect on something. Its forms are impacts, impacted and impacting. The phrase «have an impact on» is a clue that the meaning is effect, and «on impact» means at the moment of hitting.
fact: An impact is a strong hit of one thing against another.
fact: An impact is also a strong effect or influence on something.
fact: «Have an impact on» means to affect something.
fact: «Big impacts are rare but real: one blasted out Meteor Crater in Arizona.» Here impact means a hit.
fact: «Dust and gas from the impact blocked sunlight.» Here the impact caused a strong effect on the whole world.
exercise: «Big impacts are rare but real: one blasted out Meteor Crater in Arizona.» What does impacts mean here? | A quiet visit | A kind of rock that stays in the sky | A strong effect or influence | *A strong hit of one thing against another
exercise: «Exercise has a good impact on health.» What does impact mean here? | A bruise from a sports ball | A loud hit against a wall | *A strong effect on something | A sound made by a drum
exercise: Which phrase means to affect something? | Have a rest on | *Have an impact on | Make a noise on | Sit on
test: «Tsunamis can also be caused by landslides, volcanic eruptions and, very rarely, meteorite impacts.» What does impacts mean in this sentence? | *Strong hits of one thing against another | Quiet visits | Holidays by the sea | Bright lights in the sky
test: «Dust and gas from the impact blocked sunlight, plants stopped growing.» What does impact mean here? | *A strong hit and its strong effect on the world | A cloud of rain | A bright colour | A kind of plant
exam: Which meaning fits the verb «to impact» in «Rain can impact the match»? | To make a loud noise | *To have an effect on something | To hit a wall hard | To rest for a while
